/**
 * Spartrak — the 404 page's content.
 *
 * FIGMA SSOT: 1280:10788, inside the "Not Found" artboard 1280:10693.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * IT IS THE SHARED EMPTY STATE
 * ===========================================================================
 * Figma composes this page out of exactly the block the cart, the wishlist and
 * the signed-out dialog are built from — illustration, title, one explaining
 * sentence, one way out — at the larger of that component's two type steps.
 * So there is no page-specific markup here beyond the words and the
 * illustration: components/_empty-state.less owns the block and `--panel --lg`
 * picks the variant, which is the fourth caller of that component and the
 * reason it was built as one (CLAUDE.md §9).
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * FIGMA COPY TYPOS, corrected — listed so the correction is reviewable
 * ===========================================================================
 * The Arabic in 1280:10792 reads "الصفحه غير موجودة!" (الصفحه for الصفحة) and
 * 1280:10793 ends "من جديدز" (a stray ز on جديد). Both are authoring slips
 * rather than wording, and both are corrected in this theme's i18n/ar_EG.csv —
 * the same treatment, and the same reason, as the auth modal's own list of
 * four (see login-modal.phtml note e).
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHERE THE BUTTON GOES
 * ===========================================================================
 * The store home page. Figma labels it "الذهاب للتسوق" — go and shop — and
 * gives no destination. The home page is the only one that is guaranteed to
 * exist and to be the right answer for every shopper who reaches a 404,
 * whatever they were looking for; a category would be a guess about that.
 *
 * NOT `getContinueShoppingUrl()`, which the empty-cart page uses: that reads
 * the last category the shopper browsed, and someone who arrived here from an
 * external dead link has no such history to read.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * PERFORMANCE
 * ===========================================================================
 * The LCP element on this page is the 240px illustration, and it is the only
 * asset the page adds. It is a CSS background rather than an <img>, matching
 * every other caller of this component: the image is decorative — the title
 * beside it says everything it says — so it stays out of the accessibility
 * tree, and its URL is built by LESS at compile time rather than by a template
 * at render time. It is NOT lazy-loaded and NOT deferred: it is above the fold
 * on every viewport, and background images carry no `loading` attribute to get
 * wrong.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 */
?>
<div class="spartrak-empty-state spartrak-empty-state--panel spartrak-empty-state--lg">
    <span class="spartrak-empty-state__art spartrak-empty-state__art--noroute" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="spartrak-empty-state__copy">
        <strong class="spartrak-empty-state__title">
            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Page not found!')) ?>
        </strong>

        <p class="spartrak-empty-state__text">
            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Check the address you typed and try again.')) ?>
        </p>

        <a class="spartrak-empty-state__action spartrak-empty-state__action--primary"
           href="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($block->getBaseUrl()) ?>">
            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Go shopping')) ?>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>
